  "brief": "Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery have completed their acquisition, forming a new global entertainment leader called Skydance, rivaling industry giants like Netflix and YouTube.\n\nParamount / Warner Bros. Discovery (Completed): Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery Deal Completed. Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery have completed their acquisition, forming a new global entertainment leader called Skydance [1, 2, 3]. The deal brings together studios, streaming services, and cable networks under one owner, rivaling industry giants like Netflix and YouTube [2, 3, 5]. The new company, Skydance, now owns CNN and CBS News under one roof [3, 5, 7]. The acquisition was officially completed on Tuesday, following a legal battle [2, 4, 5].\nViatris / Pacira BioSciences (Announced): Viatris to Acquire Pacira BioSciences. Viatris is acquiring Pacira BioSciences for $1.65 billion [11, 12, 13]. The deal will bolster Viatris' non-opioid pain management portfolio [11, 12, 13]. Viatris will become a leader in non-opioid pain therapies after the acquisition [14].\nThird Coast / Great Plains (Announced): Third Coast and Great Plains Deal. Third Coast Bancshares, Inc. is buying Great Plains Bancshares, Inc [15, 16, 17]. The deal was announced by both companies [18]. No further information is available [16, 17, 18].\nWeston family / Boots (Announced): Weston family and Boots. The Weston family is acquiring Boots for $8.9 billion [19, 20, 21]. The deal was announced by the Weston family, with Wittington to acquire Boots [22].\nSpaceX / Nvidia (Rumored): SpaceX to Buy Nvidia Chips. SpaceX is seeking $40 billion financing to buy Nvidia chips [23, 24, 25]. Apollo and banks are in talks to finance the deal [26, 27]. The deal is reportedly led by Apollo [28]. SpaceX is also looking to raise $40 billion to buy Nvidia chips [29].\nSchneider Electric / PTC (Announced): Schneider Electric to Acquire PTC. Schneider Electric is acquiring industrial software maker PTC [30, 31, 32]. The deal is valued at $22.6 billion [31, 34, 35]. The acquisition is expected to be completed in the future [36, 37].\nMagnolia Oil & Gas / WildFire (Announced): Magnolia Oil & Gas to Acquire WildFire. Magnolia Oil & Gas is in the lead to acquire WildFire [38]. The deal is valued over $4 Billion [38]. No further information is available [38].\nKuiken Brothers / Paramus Building Supply (Completed): Kuiken Brothers Acquires Paramus Building Supply. Kuiken Brothers has acquired Paramus Building Supply [39]. The deal is now completed [39].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Mexico is betting on tech to enhance industrial platforms [40].\n- Starbucks shares plunged over 5% on chipotle acquisition rumors as Niccol's six-year tenure becomes key focus [41].\n- Eventbrite shareholders approved a $500M sale to Bending Spoons, regulatory approval pending [42].",
